   quote="Out of nine studies, eight were RCTs.",
   location="Results, paragraph 1"),
 C(id="paradigm-arms",
   what="PARADIGM-HF arm sizes against our own source-read values",
   verdict="CONFIRMED",
   detail="Their Table 1 gives 4187 and 4212. This object read 4187 and 4212 from the "
          "trial's own publication and registry record. Identical.",
   quote="McMurray et al. 2014 RCT ... 4187 ... Enalapril 10 mg twice 4212",
   location="Table 1"),
 C(id="parallel-arms",
   what="PARALLEL-HF arm sizes against our own source-read values",
   verdict="CONFIRMED",
   detail="Their Table 1 gives 111 and 112, matching this object exactly. This is the trial "
          "their list caused us to RECOVER, so their record is also the reason our k rose "
          "from two to three.",
   quote="Tsutsui et al. 2021 RCT ... 111 ... Enalapril 10 mg twice 112",
   location="Table 1"),
 C(id="prisma-arithmetic",
   what="Internal arithmetic of the study-selection flow",
   verdict="CONFIRMED",
   detail="1,066 retrieved, 985 screened after duplicates, 28 full texts, nine included. "
          "Monotone decreasing and internally consistent; no stage exceeds the one above it.",
   quote="We obtained 1,066 studies through online database searching. After removing "
         "duplicates, 985 studies were initially screened",
   location="Results, paragraph 1"),
 C(id="search-date-vs-our-newer-trial",
   what="Whether their omission of PARACHUTE-HF is an error or a date",
   verdict="CONFIRMED",
   detail="Their search closed 15 September 2023. PARACHUTE-HF reported in 2026. Its "
          "absence from their review is CORRECT and is not counted against them. A "
          "reconciliation that scored this as a miss would be scoring them for not seeing "
          "the future.",
   quote="systematically searched online databases including PubMed, Cochrane Library, and "
         "Web of Science from inception till September 15, 2023",
   location="Abstract; Methods"),
 C(id="cohort-against-own-criterion",
   what="Whether including a retrospective cohort breaches their OWN stated eligibility",
   verdict="CONFIRMED",
   detail="It does not. Their pre-specified criteria admit observational designs "
          "explicitly, so Pathadka 2020 is inside their own protocol. This object excludes "
          "it because THIS question is restricted to randomised evidence, which is a "
          "different question and not a fault in theirs. Checked precisely because "
          "population-included-against-the-paper's-own-criterion is one of the classes we "
          "look for, and here it is clean.",
   quote="The pre-defined inclusion criteria were observational studies (retrospective "
         "cohorts and prospective cohorts) or RCTs comparing sacubitril",
   location="Methods"),
 C(id="sensitivity-reported",
   what="Whether the influential non-randomised study was tested",
   verdict="CONFIRMED",
   detail="It was, and the result is reported in the body rather than buried: removing "
          "Pathadka moves all-cause mortality from 0.57 to 0.85 and heterogeneity from 94 "
          "per cent to 0. Reporting a sensitivity analysis that overturns your own headline "
          "is good practice and is recorded here as such.",
   quote="We performed sensitivity analysis by removing the study conducted by Pathadka et "
         "al. as it was a retrospective study.",
   location="Results, All-Cause Mortality"),
 C(id="no-publication-bias-test",
   what="Absence of a funnel plot or small-study test",
   verdict="CONFIRMED",
   detail="None is reported, and at nine studies none is expected: the Cochrane Handbook "
          "advises against interpreting these tests below about ten. Their omission is "
          "defensible and is NOT counted as a defect. This object applies the same caution "
          "to its own Egger's test at k = 4.",
   quote=None, location="whole paper"),
 C(id="discussion-significance-overstated",
   what="Whether the Discussion's significance claim matches the primary estimate",
   verdict="ERROR", severity="material",
   detail="The primary all-cause mortality estimate is RR 0.57 with a 95 per cent interval "
          "of 0.31 to 1.04. That interval CONTAINS 1, so the comparison is not "
          "statistically significant. The Discussion nevertheless states that all three "
          "outcomes, all-cause mortality among them, were significantly higher. The "
          "statement is true of their RCT-only sensitivity result, 0.85 (0.78 to 0.93), and "
          "is not true of the analysis the abstract leads with. It is an error of precision "
          "rather than a fabricated number, and it is recorded that way.",
   quote="The present meta-analysis reported that the risk of all-cause mortality, "
