   location="Discussion, paragraph 1"),
 C(id="abstract-headline-omits-i2",
   what="Whether the abstract's headline carries the heterogeneity it rests on",
   verdict="ERROR", severity="reporting",
   detail="The abstract reports RR 0.57 (0.31 to 1.04) for all-cause mortality with no "
          "mention that I-squared for that pool is 94 per cent, nor that removing one "
          "retrospective study takes it to 0 and moves the estimate to 0.85. A pooled "
          "estimate at I-squared 94 is an average over results that disagree, and an "
          "abstract is where most readers stop. Their own body text is transparent about "
          "both facts; the abstract is not.",
   quote="Significant heterogeneity was reported among the study results (p = 0.001; "
         "I-square: 94%).",
   location="Results, All-Cause Mortality; Abstract"),
 C(id="no-risk-of-bias-appraisal",
   what="Per-study risk-of-bias or quality appraisal",
   verdict="ABSENT",
   detail="No Cochrane RoB, Jadad, Newcastle-Ottawa or equivalent appears anywhere in the "
          "text. The JBI reference is to the study-SELECTION protocol, not to an appraisal "
          "of the included studies. Risk of bias is a required PRISMA item, and pooling a "
          "retrospective cohort with randomised trials is exactly the situation it exists "
